SUMMARY:🍽️ Book the Europe restaurant tables
DESCRIPTION:Every timed ticket and both shows are now BOOKED. What's left is restaurants:\n• The Brazen Head dinner Fri Nov 13 — book 7:30 PM so dinner runs into the ~9:30 trad session\n• The Delaunay dinner Sun Nov 15 (thedelaunay.com)\n• [DONE] Westminster Abbey Mon Nov 16, entry 12:30-1:00 — booked 24 Oct, transaction 1317740. (was: separate reminder starts Sep 20.\n• [DONE] London Eye — booked, Mon 16 Nov 3:30 PM, Fast Track x2, order 123678423\n• Gillray's dinner Mon Nov 16 (reserve a river-view table)\n• [DONE] Tue Nov 17 dinner: THE ORIGINAL IVY, 1-5 West St, 5:30 -- booked 24 Oct, OpenTable #2110431450 (replaced Royal China). Tell the server about the 7pm show. Direct line +44 20 7734 1388. Also ask if dim sum is still served at 5:30. If it never opens up, just walk in -- Chinatown on a Nov Tuesday is fine, and it's 4 min from your seats.\n• [DONE] Cursed Child — booked, Tue 17 Nov 7:00 PM, Palace Theatre, Dress Circle A19+A20, GBP 250\n• [DONE] Tower of London — booked, Wed 18 Nov (all-day ticket), order DVOMY243MYHM2\n• [DONE] Wed Nov 18 pre-theatre: BRASSERIE ZEDEL 18:00 -- booked 24 Oct, #DF2T5LTN3H3R (replaced Café Murano)\n• [DONE] Phantom of the Opera — booked, Wed 18 Nov 7:30 PM, Royal Circle A19+A20, GBP 370\n• Rules dinner Thu Nov 19 — London farewell (rules.co.uk, reserve ahead)\n• Chez Georges (first Paris dinner) Fri Nov 20 — reserve if you want a sit-down bistro (or Bouillon Chartier walk-in)\n• Le Grand Colbert dinner Sat Nov 21 — reserve (legrandcolbert.fr)\n• [DONE] Sainte-Chapelle Sun Nov 22 1:30 PM — booked 24 Oct, order ref 411040. (was: separate reminder starts Sep 25.\n• Notre-Dame free slot — reserve ~2 days ahead DURING the trip (app/site)\n• Chez Janou dinner Sun Nov 22 — reserve (chezjanou.com)\n• [DONE] Musee d'Orsay — booked, Tue 24 Nov 9:30 AM, transaction 200696183\n• La Bonne Franquette (last Paris dinner) Tue Nov 24 — reserve (or Bouillon Pigalle walk-in)\nMOST OF THESE WILL BE TOO FAR OUT UNTIL OCTOBER -- London/Paris restaurants typically open 30-60 days ahead. So work this list again in early October; nothing here is lost by waiting, and every one of them has a walk-in fallback.\n\nDONE so far: Book of Kells - Louvre - Tower of London - London Eye - Musee d'Orsay - Phantom - Cursed Child. ALL TIMED TICKETS AND BOTH SHOWS ARE BOOKED. What's left here is restaurants only.\n\n--\nTHIS REMINDER REPEATS EVERY WEEK until its deadline. Subscribed calendars are read-only, so iOS won't offer Snooze -- just dismiss it and it will come back. Once you've actually done this one, tell Claude and it gets removed from the feed for good.
