SUMMARY:🧭 Europe trip — 2-weeks-out final review
DESCRIPTION:PARIS UNREST CHECK (added 24 Oct): after the 17 Oct riots Paris ran an 11pm-6am curfew at Place de la Republique + part of Les Halles (rue Rambuteau / rue Berger / bd de Sebastopol) and closed Chatelet, Les Halles and Republique metro stations from 10pm on protest weekends. Your hotel (123 bd de Sebastopol) is ~10 min walk NORTH of that zone. Check: (1) is any curfew still in force, and does it reach the hotel? (2) any strike/march dates for 20-25 Nov -- esp. SNCF/Eurostar on Fri 20 and Saturday 21 (Louvre was blockaded by students on 19 Oct); (3) US Embassy Paris alerts (fr.usembassy.gov) + STEP enrolment; (4) RATP closures for late dinners near Chatelet. None of this needs action now.\n\nPlaybook checklist: re-verify every venue's hours/closed-days/closures for our dates; confirm all reservations & timed tickets are booked + saved offline; swap weather averages for the live forecast; DOWNLOAD OFFLINE MAPS for Dublin, London and Paris in Google Maps -- phones are locked to T-Mobile so there is no travel eSIM, and offline maps are the single biggest data saver. Also turn ON WiFi Calling and turn OFF photo backup over cellular. Plan confirmed: Go5G Plus, ~15GB high-speed each (30GB between you), then unlimited at reduced speed. Nothing to buy in advance; top up in-app only if you somehow run out (~$35 for 15GB/10 days). (Travel insurance: DECLINED 6 Sep -- self-insuring, no need to revisit.) Since you're self-insured: call your health plan before you fly and ask exactly what it covers in Ireland/UK/France, and save the answer offline. Emergency number is 112 across all three (999 also works in UK and Ireland). Abroad you pay up front -- keep every receipt and itemised bill.\n\nNEW (Sept re-route): you now clear US customs at PHILADELPHIA on the way home (Nov 25), not Charlotte. You both have GLOBAL ENTRY, so no app needed - just confirm both Known Traveler Numbers are on the AA booking so PreCheck prints on the boarding passes. Also: the return lands Tampa 11:51 PM, the night before Thanksgiving - sort out parking or a pickup.\n\n--\nTHIS REMINDER REPEATS EVERY 2 DAYS until its deadline. Subscribed calendars are read-only, so iOS won't offer Snooze -- just dismiss it and it will come back. Once you've actually done this one, tell Claude and it gets removed from the feed for good.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Europe trip final review — verify openings & bookings  (repeats until done)
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
