SUMMARY:🛂 Lenny's UK ETA (Aaron's done) + Global Entry numbers on the AA booking
DESCRIPTION:AARON'S UK ETA IS APPROVED (24 Oct). LENNY'S IS STILL NEEDED before boarding BA Dublin-London on Sun 15 Nov -- a boarding requirement, not a formality. The Common Travel Area exemption does NOT cover Americans visiting Ireland.\n\nLENNY CAN DO IT WITHOUT AARON:\n- Easiest: Lenny installs the 'UK ETA' app (developer: UK Home Office) on their own phone and applies -- scans the passport + face, about 10 minutes.\n- Or Aaron applies on the website (apply-for-an-eta.homeoffice.gov.uk, via gov.uk/eta) using a photo of Lenny's passport photo page and a face photo Lenny sends.\nGBP 20, decision usually within a day but can take up to 3 working days -- so do it by ~10 Nov at the latest.\n!! Only gov.uk / homeoffice.gov.uk or the official app. uk.eta.travel and similar are third-party resellers.\n\nWHILE THE PASSPORTS ARE OUT, check both:\n1. EXPIRY after 25 FEB 2027.\n2. ISSUE DATE after ~25 NOV 2016 (Schengen 10-year rule).\n\nALSO: add both Global Entry KNOWN TRAVELER NUMBERS to AA reservation APNJVO (aa.com > your trip > passenger details, or 800-433-7300) so TSA PreCheck prints on the boarding passes.\n\n(ETIAS is NOT required -- not launched.)\n\n--\nREPEATS EVERY 2 DAYS until done. Tell Claude once Lenny's is approved and it comes out of the feed.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Lenny's UK ETA + add Global Entry KTNs to AA  (repeats until done)
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
